<speak>Your aim is to reduce your technology-sector concentration and make your portfolio less sensitive to swings in that sector. I recommend reducing your holding in Nova Technology Equity Fund because it focuses on technology companies, so reducing it directly addresses your aim of lowering technology-sector exposure. You may lose part or even all of the capital you invested, and disposing of the holding can crystallise a loss. The transaction charge is 0.3%. Are you willing to accept an investment loss when reducing this holding?</speak>